From 2871b27ee46c0a29d6bc712b78ff31a2eecc75f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:05:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel behaviours: one definition of the time step
 scaling factor of the statistics

On all the backends, the time step scaling factor of the statistics given
by the execution options is the minimum of their initial value and of the
factors of the points which are lower than the initial value of the batch.
The backends updating the statistics by atomic operations already did so.
The `stlpar`, `openmp` and `openacc` backends merged the factor of the
batch even if no point lowered it: statistics initialized with a factor
greater than the one of the batch were lowered, for instance by the
rotations, which use `1`.

The rotations never lower the time step scaling factor and leave the
statistics unchanged on all the backends: this is tested by the
comparison with the `generic` interface.
